## Progress

- **12:45** First working layout. Placement is done one window at a time —
  each terminal spawned with its own `--app-id`, polled for in the sway tree,
  then explicitly focused before splitting off the next. Brave is launched
  into a throwaway holder pane and swapped into its slot once its window
  appears, so its slow startup cannot scramble the tree.
- **12:47** Bug: the 40/60 split kept coming out inverted. `focus` and
  `resize` sent as two separate `swaymsg` calls are not atomic and brave
  grabbed focus in between, so the resize hit the browser. All geometry
  commands now carry `[con_id=…]` criteria instead of relying on focus.
- **12:47** Self-inflicted: a runtime `for_window [class="…"]` rule for beeper
  matched native Wayland windows (which have no X11 class) and vacuumed
  workspace 1 into the scratchpad. Reverted, workspace restored to its exact
  original tabbed layout, and the permanent rule in the sway config matches on
  `app_id` only.
- **12:49** Repo created at ~/ŻYCIE/VIBECODING/go-layout, pushed public.
  ~/.local/bin/go-layout symlinked into it so edits are live.
- **13:10** `--fresh` made the default: build on the lowest empty workspace
  rather than always workspace 1, since on an occupied tabbed workspace the
  whole layout nested itself into a single new tab. Surfaced two more bugs —
  a second `go` latched onto the first run's `go-r1` (app_ids now tagged with
  the run's PID), and brave activating an old window dragged focus back to
  the wrong workspace (focus is now claimed last).
- **13:30** `go` did nothing at all in a real terminal — three silent
  failures stacked: `setsid -f` lost the race against the terminal closing
  and was killed before executing a line; `swaymsg exec go-layout` found
  nothing because sway's PATH has no ~/.local/bin, and reported success
  anyway; and the closing terminal dragged focus back after the workspace
  switch. Launcher now goes through sway with an absolute path, and the
  script asserts the workspace switch and moves the anchor pane if sway put
  it elsewhere. Logging switched to per-line append so a killed run leaves a
  trace instead of vanishing.
- **14:09** Verified beeper end to end, both launched by `go` and launched
  independently: parked in the scratchpad at 1200x800 either way, no loose
  window on any workspace.

